  "issue": 521,
  "request": "Goal: Fix the mismatch between sennel flow parser contracts and displayed help. Scope: Extend the existing CommandDefinition and FLOW_COMMANDS as the single option authority; derive leaf and direct-child group help from typed option models; share the three public group-help render paths with deterministic ordering and visible spacing; inventory per-leaf inputs and reuse existing validators, target guards, runtime-path rules, and lifecycle behavior; preserve flow query as its separate parser exception; add exhaustive routed registry/parser contract coverage and focused CLI integration/E2E coverage. Out of scope: changing command semantics, target-guard decisions, runtime directory behavior, or query behavior; adding blanket validation or arbitrary new limits; treating unresolved revision 008 as approved. Description: Follow Issue 521's authoritative Restart contract from flow review dated 2026-09-24 for the initial Draft and Spec, superseding historical counts and wording. Re-enumerate current registry contracts and map each retained public surface to its owner and tests.",
